y sweet and really lovely  how did you and katie come up with the  name eloise and did you bring a picture  or two this morning  well it took about three days for us to  come up with the name  she she is waking up by the day by the  second  uh she's she she is uh opening her eyes  she's turning when she hears our voices  she'll grab our fingers she clasps her  hands  i am savoring this gail in such a way  you know i've been here before  yeah it's my fourth child life moves  fast  i can't believe i'm at this point it's  the last time and i'm just soaking up  every moment of it ugh i love it i'm so  in love katie's so in love  she is doing an incredible job  sustaining that child right now as we  speak the babies inside i was going to  do this shoot in my house  uh surrounded by baby debris uh  burping claws and uh sean our our  intrepid executive producer was like  sending me a text message can we please  just do it in a truck where it's gonna  look neat and orderly fine fine  but that's not weird she wants it to  look neat and note to self tony it's not  called baby debris  yet it's called baby accoutrements for  dad's debris  for dads it's a break tony  congratulations speaking of  go ahead thank you thank you i want to  say one more thing that speaking of  baby debris one of her latest tricks is  she can smile  now i am aware that the smile is tied to  baby debris in the diaper  but it is a beautiful and wonderful  thing anyway awesome all right tony  thanks so much you can see  tony's report thanks guys defend  treasure on 48 hours tomorrow night at  10  9 central here on cbs

